    "title": "What California viewers need to know to watch 2026 Players Championship",
    "text": "March 12, 2026, 9:02 a.m. PTIt's a good time to be alive if you're a golf fan. The 2026 Players Championship started today.TPC Sawgrass always provides immaculate views and even better golf. This year should be no different, with dozens of contenders set to tee off soon, including Scottie Scheffler, Rory McIlroy, Collin Morikawa, and Brooks Koepka, among many others.McIlroy is playing in the event despite a back injury he suffered at the Arnold Palmer Invitational. That's the kind of dedication to expect at The Players Championship. After all, McIlroy has some pretty decent incentives. Both he and Scottie Scheffler are just one win away from joining Jack Nicklaus as the only golfers in history with three wins at The Players Championship.TPC Sawgrass is known for being unforgiving, though. One slip-up could ruin a round. This is the tournament where consistency will win above all else, and that makes it all the more exciting.Here's how to watch the 2026 Players Championship from California.How to watch Round 1 of 2026 Players ChampionshipThe first round of the 2026 Players Championship started streaming exclusively on ESPN+ starting at 4:30 a.m. PT. Television coverage of the event will begin at 10 a.m. PT on Golf Channel. Both ESPN+ and Golf Channel will provide coverage of Round 1 through 4 p.m. PT. You can also listen on listen in on Sirius XM starting at 9 a.m.The Players Championship first round tee times, groups*All times listed are Pacific Standard Time (PT)No. 1 tee4:40 a.m. – Mark Hubbard, Thorbjørn Olesen, Mac Meissner4:52 a.m. – Bud Cauley, Vince Whaley, Chandler Phillips5:04 a.m. – Emiliano Grillo, Christiaan Bezuidenhout, Max Greyserman5:16 a.m. – Kevin Yu, Cam Davis, Gary Woodland5:28 a.m. – Ricky Castillo, Ryan Gerard, Patrick Cantlay5:40 a.m. – Adam Schenk, Garrick Higgo, Matt McCarty5:52 a.m. – Brian Harman, Maverick McNealy, Davis Riley6:04 a.m. – Sami Valimaki, Lucas Glover, Matt Fitzpatrick6:16 a.m. – Michael Brennan, Harris English, 